+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  The optional :rst:dir:`canonical` option gives the
+   alias expression; names in the expression are parsed as Python type
+   references.
+
+   .. code-block:: rst
+
+      .. py:type:: Alias
+         :canonical: list[Target]
+
+   The directive supports the same description body as other Python object
+   directives.  Type aliases can be referenced with :rst:role:`py:type` or
+   the generic :rst:role:`py:obj` role.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      The optional alias expression, displayed after the alias name and parsed
+      using Python type annotation syntax.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:exception:: name
                    .. py:exception:: name(parameters)
